  spider-man is vulture ever since we got  the morbius trailer we have found out  that vulture not only exists within the  marvel cinematic universe but he also  exists in the sp  umc as well and for those of you who may  not know that is the sony picture  universe of marvel characters the same  universe that tom hardy's venom is in  but here's something that's very  interesting about michael keaton's  vulture appearance in the morbius  trailer  now in the morbius trailer it really  does look like adrian tombs most people  would say without a doubt this is the  same vulture from spider-man homecoming  but in the morbius trailer there's also  a picture of spider-man on the wall  on it it says murderer over it now of  course this is a callback to the  post-credits scene of spider-man far  from home where jay jonah jameson and  mysterio make spider-man slash peter  parker out to be a murderer however the  spider-man on the wall  is not actually tom holland's spider-man  it's tobey maguire spider-man from the  sam raimi series  now a lot of people thought that this  could be due to some type of rights  issues between  sony and marvel however if a real-life  spider-verse is coming this could  actually be toby maguire spider-man  instead of tom holland being spider-man  in this universe it's toby maguire but  some of the same  incidents and events could happen to him  in this universe  so what exactly does this mean well  during the time where we had that whole  spider-man scare between  sony and disney which was definitely  very nerve-wracking but when it came to  an end and disney and sony worked out a  deal kevin feige the president of marvel  studios came out and said that  spider-man  our spider-man tom holland was the only  marvel character currently  that had the ability to jump between  universes now obviously he didn't mean  that as in he has magical powers like  doctor strange can open up a portal and  go to a different universe  that's not what he meant so what he  really meant was tom holland spider-man  is going to be interacting with other  characters  from other different universes mainly  sony's universe the sony picture  universe of marvel characters and  the amazing spider-man universe and some  other blatant evidence of this as j  jonah jameson making his appearance in  the mcu  and of course this is not a new ga jonah  jameson this is the same j  jonah jameson from the original  spider-man sam remy trilogy  played by jk simmons again like i said  if it's a new version of a character  simply in a different  film you get another actor but instead  we have the classic jk  simmons j jonah jameson who is now in  the mcu but  coming from the original sam raimi  universe this combined with the sam  raimi spider-man in the morbius trailer  gives us a connection to three different  universes this  is sam raimi's universe connecting with  morbius but also sam raimi's universe  connecting with the marvel cinematic  universe  and to top it all off vulture is in the  morbius trailer as well so the marvel  cinematic universe connects with the sp  umc  so those are three universes that we  already have evidence are intertwining  with each other  and now you take into consideration the  fact that jamie foxx's electro from the  amazing spider-man 2  is going to show up in spider-man 3 in  the mcu means that we have  four different spider-man universes  colliding  and this is the real life spider-verse  now of course this is  insanely cool and we've actually had a  few reports about this in the past which  i'll go over in just a second but right  now the question is  why is this actually going to happen  besides the fact that everybody would  just simply lose their minds but there  does have to be sort of a reason for  andrew garfield spider-man and toby  mcguire spider-man to team up with tom  holland or have a good reason to  at the very least make a cameo now  moving forward it looks like sony and  disney are actually playing very nicely  with each other and some little things  have slipped out here and there like  olivia wilde being hired to direct a new  spider-man movie that's going to be  based off of a woman spider-man  it hasn't yet been confirmed if it's  going to be spider woman or spider gwen  but olivia wilde did make some comments  that lead us to believe  that this movie might actually be a  marvel sony movie and will take place  inside of the mcu  so this would be a fourth piece to this  new live-action spider-verse either  having spider-woman or spider-gwen  and let's also not forget that marvel is  once again working with  sam raimi the director of the original  spider-man trilogy with tobey maguire  a while ago marvel studios hired sam  remy to direct doctor strange in the  multiverse of madness which is very  fitting if the real-life spider-verse is  indeed going to happen because the  multiverse is going to essentially blow  up in doctor strange in the multiverse  of madness  and that leads us to the question when  exactly is all of this going to happen  when are we going to see the live-action  spider-verse well there are two ways  that this could actually happen  one is that marvel studios and sony  could simply do  projects that exist inside of the same  universe having different characters  from different projects cross over into  other projects that they're working on  together this would be pretty cool as it  would be an  ongoing process and we'd see many  characters interact with each other  over essentially years so it wouldn't  just be a one and done type of thing it  would be something that would last for a  while and as mikey sutton from geekosti  has reported recently  a lot of these spider-man spin-off  projects are going to exist in the same  universe  but of course they could also do a  pretty big project and have a real-life  spider-verse movie now this would not be  spider-man 3. there is a possibility for  cameos from andrew garfield and toby  maguire in spider-man 3 but as far as a  huge  movie where the spider-verse is  established that's not going to be  spider-man 3  but we could get a setup for it in  spider-man 3. because you have to keep  in mind from what we know the new deal  between sony and disney is for tom  holland to do one more  solo spider-man film and then another  team-up film now for the team-up film we  all assume that it's going to be an  avengers team-up film  but what if it's not what if it's  actually a spider-man spider-verse film  it's certainly a possibility considering  all the evidence that we have or perhaps  this is something that marvel and sony  are going to want to build up  over time and eventually release to the  public but either way there's just a ton  of evidence that leads us to believe  that toby maguire andrew garfield  and tom holland will eventually be in  the same movie together  especially if you consider the fact that  the wanda vision series looks like it's  going to bend reality in a very  different way  and perhaps it could be the reason why  the multiverse is in madness for doctor  strange too  whatever it may be one thing is for sure  there are so many exciting things coming  to the future  of the mcu so let me know what you would  like to see happen would you like a  real-life spider-verse  movie or would you like to see a bunch  of different movies all exist within the  same universe and characters crossing  over  let me know what you think in the  comments down below don't forget to like  this video and subscribe so you don't  miss out on any of the marvel videos for  live updates you can follow me on  instagram and twitter and as always  thank you all so much for watching  woof  you

